Author: Nxeon <haxkodi@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Sep 19 16:46:40 2026 +0000

    Fix NxLabs: real server-side pagination past the 400-mod cap, portal homepage hero

    listCatalogMods() capped every query at 400 rows (a documented Phase 1
    stopgap) with no page 2 — scripts/import-modrinth-catalog.ts's real bulk
    import landed 32,251 minecraft mods, leaving ~31,850 of them permanently
    unreachable across all four StoreBrowser call sites (marketing + portal,
    cross-game + per-family).

    Replaced listCatalogMods/searchCatalogMods with queryCatalogMods(), real
    DB-level pagination/search/sort/category-filter (skip/take off a real
    count()), reusing lib/pagination.ts's existing paginate() helper (extended
    with buildHref()) the same way /blog and the admin tables already do.
    Search moved fully server-side, not just paging: the search box's own
    placeholder promises to search the catalogue, and the chips already
    advertised real DB-wide counts a client-side filter over one loaded page
    couldn't honor at this scale. StoreBrowser is now a Server Component --
    search/sort/chips/pager are plain links and a native GET form, no client JS
    required. Added listCategoryCounts()/totalDownloadsFor() so per-family stat
    rows stay accurate instead of being derived from whichever page was loaded.

    Also gave the portal NxLabs homepage (app/dashboard/nxlabs/page.tsx) the
    hero image its own sibling per-family page already has via PageShell's
    existing heroImage slot -- no shell change needed, just wiring the prop.

    npx tsc --noEmit clean. Documented in docs/DOCUMENTATION.md.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

